Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imx95: respect Raven M7 resource ownership
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [embedded specific]

Linux must not probe M7 peripherals or its eDMA channels. The unmasked
upper eDMA channels cause an asynchronous SError in fsl_edma_probe.
Validated with equivalent U-Boot FDT edits through Raven's Linux login prompt.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-15x15-frdm.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-15x15-frdm.dts
@@ -1255,3 +1255,37 @@
 			       <361267200>, <49152000>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/* Raven SM assigns these resources to M7. */
+&gpio2 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&adc1 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&lpspi3 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&flexcan1 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&flexcan2 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&flexcan5 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&tpm1 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&edma2 {
+	/* Mask SM channels 0/1 and Raven M7 channels 32..63. */
+	dma-channel-mask = <0x00000003 0xffffffff>;
+};
